  "id": "perceptualmotor-coordination-v2-4ffa616260",
  "term": "perceptual–motor coordination",
  "definition": "Perceptual–motor coordination is the synchronization and organization of a person's movements with perceived environmental events or with another person's actions, typically through visual, haptic, or auditory information. In interpersonal contexts, it involves dynamic mutual influence between co-actors as they adapt their actions in time.",
